  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking bug**:\n\n**[P1] `canEdit` checks READ instead of WRITE — `src/guard.js:12`**\nJavaScript evaluates `===` before `&`, so `share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` becomes `share.mask & true`, effectively checking bit 1 (READ).\n\nOn an unlocked document:\n- A view-only share (`mask: 1`) **can edit**.\n- A WRITE-only share (`mask: 4`) **cannot edit**.\n\nUse `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`, consistent with the other guards. Add regression tests for those two cases—the existing editor test has both READ and WRITE, so it misses this.\n\nAll 6 existing tests pass; I reproduced the bug with additional read-only checks. No code or files changed.",
